# Citation metadata for MATL (https://citation-file-format.github.io). GitHub shows a
# "Cite this repository" button generated from this file.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MATL in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "MATL: Matrix Algebra Template Library"
abstract: >-
  MATL is a header-only C++20 library for dense matrix algebra with syntax close to
  the mathematics. Expressions are evaluated lazily with expression templates, matrix
  products use a cache-blocked SIMD kernel, and temporaries are recycled so that
  repeated evaluations make no heap allocations.
authors:
  - family-names: Fust
    given-names: Daniel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9950-5047"
version: 2.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/DanielFust/MATL"
keywords:
  - linear algebra
  - matrix
  - expression templates
  - C++20
  - header-only
  - high-performance computing
